From: android-kitkat-tls12 <android-kitkat-tls12@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 22/30] Cycle guard for the learned-intermediate loop of
 02e4d22 (TrustManagerImpl)

cm-11 02e4d22 (= conscrypt 04e7d1d, libcore/0015) caches the
intermediates of every validated chain in intermediateIndex and, in
step 2 of cleanupCertChainAndFindTrustAnchors, appends the cached
issuer of the last certificate until there is none. The loop has no
"already used" check. When two cached intermediates issue each other
(a cross-signed pair) and the index returns them first for their
subjects, the walk never ends: the chain array doubles until the VM
runs out of memory. cm-11 and AOSP 6.0.1 ship the loop in this form;
Android 7.0 replaced it with a path builder that keeps a set of used
certificates.

This keeps the 4.4 loop and adds such a set: it starts with the
certificates of the presented chain that step 1 ordered, and the walk
stops at the first certificate it has already used. Steps 3 and 5 then
run as before on the chain built so far. The walk takes the first
cached issuer only and does not backtrack, so a leaf whose first cached
issuer leads into the cycle is rejected (trust anchor not found) where
7.0 would try another issuer; before this change the same check never
returned.

Test: TrustManagerImplTest.testLearnedIntermediateCrossSignedPairTerminates.
CAs I and J cross-sign each other (I_J, J_I) and I also has a
certificate from the trusted root (I_R). The valid chain L, I_J, J_I,
I_R teaches the trust manager I_J, J_I and I_R in that order, so the
bare leaf L is completed as L, I_J, J_I, I_J, ... The check runs in a
worker thread with a 60 s limit; before this change it does not
terminate, now it fails with a CertificateException, and the chains
through I_R still validate.

Android 4.3 port (android-4.3_r3) of patch 0022 of the 4.4 series. Paths
and names: libcore/crypto of 4.4 (org.conscrypt,
org_conscrypt_NativeCrypto.cpp in libjavacrypto) is libcore/luni on 4.3
(org.apache.harmony.xnet.provider.jsse,
org_apache_harmony_xnet_provider_jsse_NativeCrypto.cpp in libjavacore).
Otherwise the same change; only line offsets differ.
---
 .../xnet/provider/jsse/TrustManagerImpl.java  |  11 ++
 .../provider/jsse/TrustManagerImplTest.java   | 111 ++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 122 insertions(+)

diff --git a/luni/src/main/java/org/apache/harmony/xnet/provider/jsse/TrustManagerImpl.java b/luni/src/main/java/org/apache/harmony/xnet/provider/jsse/TrustManagerImpl.java
index 3b73fc064..45a22008a 100644
--- a/luni/src/main/java/org/apache/harmony/xnet/provider/jsse/TrustManagerImpl.java
+++ b/luni/src/main/java/org/apache/harmony/xnet/provider/jsse/TrustManagerImpl.java
@@ -368,6 +368,13 @@ public final class TrustManagerImpl implements X509TrustManager {
         }
 
         // 2. Add any missing intermediates to the chain
+        // kktls: never add a certificate twice. Cached intermediates that issue each other (a
+        // cross-signed pair) would otherwise grow the chain until the VM runs out of memory.
+        // Android 7.0 keeps a set of used certificates for the same reason.
+        Set<X509Certificate> used = new HashSet<X509Certificate>();
+        for (int i = 0; i <= currIndex; i++) {
+            used.add(chain[i]);
+        }
         while (true) {
             TrustAnchor nextIntermediate =
                     intermediateIndex.findByIssuerAndSignature(chain[currIndex]);
@@ -376,6 +383,10 @@ public final class TrustManagerImpl implements X509TrustManager {
             }
             // Append intermediate
             X509Certificate cert = nextIntermediate.getTrustedCert();
+            if (!used.add(cert)) {
+                // kktls: a cycle; stop here and let steps 3 and 5 look for an anchor.
+                break;
+            }
             // don't mutate original chain, which may be directly from an SSLSession
             if (chain == original) {
                 chain = original.clone();
